<table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 27, 2004 :: Grats Zelcon on your fancy shmancy shawl!!</div><P>Thanks all for coming for a quick run over to do the shawl war for Zelcon after killing the fatty fast! This time we just had Mahrsan walk the General where we wanted him, with the General doing his best to kill our fearless monk in the process! </P>
<P>In the end, it was one very happy kitty with a fancy new shawl! Grats Zelcon!! </P>
<P>Think I've missed these levels...</P>
<P>Grats Valkyra on 65 and Prophet!<BR>Grats Cimmy and Dorina on 64!<BR>Grats Tankorr on 63!<BR>Grats Ladibugg on 61!<BR>Grats Grellik on 55 (prob higher by now)<BR>Grats Reivan on 54!<BR>Grats BUfo and Thiia on 46!</P>
<P>And I leave you with a scary image....<BR><IMG alt=Aeeieeeeaaaa!!! hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/shatta.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Jan 28, 2004</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 24, 2004 :: Terris Thule takes a nap!</div><P>Had to finish with our task of saving Balut from Nightmares, so we headed into her lair and knocked her down. Grats Kleria and Ccra on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/KnuckleboneBeadedVeil.gif">Knucklebone Beaded Veils</A>! </P>
<P><IMG alt="Not so pretty dead!" hspace=0 src="http://nibbler.servepics.com/capulus/uploads/meeka/terris.jpg" align=baseline border=0></P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 23, 2004 :: Falling behind again!</div><P>Some more folks have leveled, and I don't have a list in front of me! I'm sure another officer will edit those in *hint hint*</P>
<P>Killed the pretty white dragon in his tower again. Grats Raihndance on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/yelinaks_talisman.JPG">his talisman</A>, Vorne on <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/yelinakshead.jpg">his head</A>, Zavitar saved <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/Celestial_Essence_Robe.jpg">a robe</A> from rotting, Punkgurl saved <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics16/craslith.jpg">a sword</A> from the same fate and Ceyria saved <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/sacrifice.jpg">a mace</A> as well. Kasserole won <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics15/maskofthedragonslayer.jpg">the mask</A> on greed rolls! </P>
<P>Headed into Sleepers and got the elusive <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/Ancient_Prismatic_Bow.jpg">Prismatic Bow</A> to drop. Wait, that's not accurate... got THREE of the damn things to drop. Grats Beryllin, Antroe and Papajay! Cerdiwan got his <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/Ancient_Prismatic_Axe.jpg">Prismatic Axe</A>, Anarandil got his much desired <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/ancientprismaticclaymore.jpg">Claymore</A> and Divan got a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/Ancient_Prismatic_Stiletto.jpg">Stiletto</A>! Got more quest stuff and Wonderous got the last peice needed to finish the quest on our next trip in! Jenrenee also got a <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/eyeofthederanged.gif">nifty ranged item</A> for fun too! </P>
<P>&nbsp;</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 20, 2004 :: Dead Xanny for fun!</div><P>Thanks to Wonderous for planning&nbsp;Xanny and Mahrsan for taking over running it when Wonderbuns had carpool issues and was late! Nice work all! Course, I realized as we were doing it that I don't think more than 1 of us needed the flag. /chuckles</P>
<P>Grats Kasserole on the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/CordHiltedSpikeDriver.gif">Cord Hilted Spike Driver</A> and Spark on the <A href="http://everquest.allakhazam.com/equipment/graphics19/PulsingPhaseEmitter.gif">Phase Pulse Emitter thingy of goodness</A>!! Not bad for an hour of work :)</P>
<P>Grats Iionz on 61!<BR>Grats Thrakish on 51 and Primalist!<BR>Grats Bufo on 42!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 18, 2004 :: Dragons and Fun!</div><P>We had a busy week! We managed to take down an additional three First Brood dragons! Congrats to Zavitar and Cerdiwan! </P>
<P>Meeka edit: Oops, and belated grats Arid on your prismatic, and Mah on getting the elusive fistwraps and Papa on skull on a stick bonus weapon! Also belated grats to Jenrenee on Yel's talisman, Grajin on his head, me on a robe nobody wanted and Perragon,&nbsp;Wellish and Desultor nabbing some toys! I now return you to the rest of Wond's edit.. Oh! After saying thanks to Wond for leading the west coasters out to kill Vindi after us east coasters sat back and relaxed. Well, or went to bed so we could get up for work. Something like that. </P>
<P>We've had quite a few levels as well!</P>
<OL>
<LI>Bufo 40th! 
<LI>Punkgurl 62nd! 
<LI>Milora 59th! 
<LI>Dalorm 56th! 
<LI>Wellish the High Priest at 60th!! 
<LI>Turtleman 45th! 
<LI>Speid 40th!</LI></OL>
<P>Keep up the levels everyone! It shall be an interesting week!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Wonderous<br> :: Last edited by Meeka on Jan 20, 2004</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 15, 2004 :: More levels and dragons</div><P>Ran and killed another dragon fastlike to get Aridius his Sleepers Key finally, go go bard power! Then we ran and showed Kelerok'Dar what massive overkill was really like. We let Nefarius tank! </P>
<P>Grats Edko on 65 and Archon!<BR>Grats Brytelyte on 62! <BR>Grats Punkgurl on 61!<BR>Grats Snot on 53!<BR>Grats Thrakish on 50! (did I already get this one?)<BR>Grats Tman on 44!<BR>Grats Emanci on Sensei!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 13, 2004 :: Welcome to our newest officer!</div><P>Welcome to Arglar, Cimerene and BOB.. err.. Jakr as our newest officers! We will arrange a time to punt Arglar to celebrate soon!</P>
<P>These were some of the levels I missed...<BR>Grats Raining on 65 and Arcanist!<BR>Grats Zorin on 62!<BR>Grats Thrakish on 48!<BR>Grats Turtleman on 43!<BR>Grats Bashiuss on Sir!</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><table class="news-table" border="1" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><tr><td><div class="title-text">Jan 12, 2004 :: Rings and Kings</div><P>Another relaxing Ring War... no, this time it wasn't an evil one! I got to chat and relax mostly on bard duty! </P>
<P>Grats Emanci on your 10th Ring, Zelcon on your Crown of Narandi and Thayet on your Choker of the Wretched! None of the heroes died, but I forget exactly who got the rest of those loots. </P>
<P>After all that nice coldain faction work, we decided to go stuff the Dain for his head! Who says you need to bring DPS to that fight? /rolls eyes </P>
<P>Anyways... grats Mahrsan on Dain's head and you're swanky new belt! Reide saved the tri-plated hammer of instant clicking shielding goodness from rot, Vorne saved the Aegis of Ice from rot, and two others got the Frostreavers Cloak and Ring of Winter on greed. Seriously, great fun fight! Shows how determined we are. </P>
<P>I know there are some levels that should go here...</P><p class="lastedit"> :: Posted by Meeka</p></td></tr></table><p /><span class="page-scroll">Pages: <a href='news.asp?page=3'>&laquo;</a>&nbsp;<a href='news.asp?page=1'>1</a> <a href='news.asp?page=2'>2</a> <a href='news.asp?page=3'>3</a> 4 <a href='news.asp?page=5'>5</a> <a href='news.asp?page=6'>6</a>...<a href='news.asp?page=13'>13</a>&nbsp;<a href='news.asp?page=5'>&raquo;</a></span></td>
